<p>Pakistan has moved to shore up a possible mediation effort between the United States and Iran, holding talks with China in Beijing to refine a framework for dialogue. Pakistani officials say they are prepared to help host negotiations aimed at de-escalation. Multiple outlets say Pakistan is drawing on its ties with both Washington and Tehran, while China has publicly backed Islamabad’s effort to lower tensions. The stakes go well beyond bilateral diplomacy. Pakistani officials and analysts say a prolonged conflict involving Iran would directly threaten Pakistan’s economy and internal security, while regional observers quoted by the outlets are divided over whether a peaceful settlement is still within reach. Even though the chances of actual US-Iran talks remain uncertain, the latest contacts in Beijing show that regional players are still looking for a diplomatic off-ramp, leaving at least a narrow opening for dialogue in a dangerous standoff.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/vYCG6FZwWLaj6HohbSgZgz-2XmGNSzUzddb3q8f1hKZEhpHQ2Kq68rj-MKMLQ0ykw4pvG-0lO_gASrcgJKacCIaw13SUuaKkf1-UOg-gP4B7' alt='Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Ishaq Dar meets Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi in Beijing on Jan 4, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Framework first: The Beijing contacts are focused on shaping a possible format for dialogue before any direct US-Iran negotiations are confirmed, which shows how preliminary the effort still is.</li><li>Pressure to deliver: DW’s coverage says Islamabad is under pressure not just to offer mediation, but to make any hosted diplomacy look credible and useful.</li><li>Headwinds remain: The Christian Science Monitor says Pakistan’s access to both Washington and Tehran may open doors, but it does not remove the major obstacles facing any mediator.</li><li>Talks still unclear: NDTV described the prospect of actual US-Iran negotiations as &#x27;nebulous,&#x27; a reminder that the current push is still short of a confirmed negotiating track.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pakistan government: Islamabad is presenting itself as both a potential venue and a mediator, signaling that it wants a concrete host in place if talks materialize. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-under-pressure-to-host-successful-us-iran-talks/a-76596163'>DW</a>)</li><li>China: Beijing is positioning itself as a backer of Pakistan’s de-escalation push, publicly supporting the initiative rather than taking the mediator role for itself. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/pakistan-envoy-to-visit-china-as-us-iran-talks-remain-nebulous-11289399#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Regional analysts: Commentators cited by The Christian Science Monitor say Pakistan’s real advantage is access to both capitals, but they caution that access alone may not overcome the headwinds facing mediation. (<a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Asia-South-Central/2026/0330/pakistan-mediator-us-iran-war'>The Christian Science Monitor</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera panelists: The discussion focuses more on political feasibility than process, asking whether any peaceful settlement is still realistic under current conditions. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/inside-story/2026/3/30/is-a-peaceful-settlement-possible-in-iran-2'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1987057/pak-china-talks-in-beijing-to-refine-framework-for-possible-us-iran-dialogue'>Pak-China talks in Beijing to ‘refine’ framework for possible US-Iran dialogue</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-under-pressure-to-host-successful-us-iran-talks/a-76596163'>Pakistan under pressure to host successful US-Iran talks</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/inside-story/2026/3/30/is-a-peaceful-settlement-possible-in-iran-2'>Is a peaceful settlement possible in Iran?</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/pakistan-envoy-to-visit-china-as-us-iran-talks-remain-nebulous-11289399#publisher=newsstand'>Pakistan Envoy To Visit China As US-Iran Talks Remain Nebulous</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Asia-South-Central/2026/0330/pakistan-mediator-us-iran-war'>Why Pakistan has emerged as key mediator in US-Iran war</a> - csmonitor.com</li></ul>